    "result_text": "The full test suite passes. `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class (the other files under `acceptance/` are the abstract base and a support class), and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented idempotent owner creation in `OwnerRestControllerV1` (which serves `POST /api/owners`).\n\n**What changed** (`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n\n- Added an in-memory `ConcurrentHashMap<String, Integer> idempotentCreates` mapping a seen `Idempotency-Key` to the id of the owner its first successful create produced.\n- Reworked `addOwner(...)`:\n  - Reads the `Idempotency-Key` header from the current request (via `RequestContextHolder` \u2014 the method signature is fixed by the OpenAPI-generated `OwnersApi` interface, so the header can't be added as a parameter).\n  - If the key was already seen and the owner still exists, it returns that original owner with **200 OK** instead of creating a duplicate.\n  - Otherwise it runs the normal create pipeline; on a successful **201 Created**, it records `key \u2192 new owner id` so a later repeat hits the idempotent path.\n- Added a small `currentIdempotencyKey()` helper that returns the non-blank header value or `null`.\n\n**Behavior matches the spec and the `coreIdempotentRepeat` test:** the first create returns 2xx, the repeat with the same key returns 200 with the same owner id \u2014 no duplicate (which the duplicate-household rule would otherwise reject with 409). Requests without the header keep their existing behavior. Reading the header is null-safe when no request is bound to the thread.",
