    "probe_text": "The subagent's map matches the code exactly. Here is the complete ordered list of everything that happens on `POST /api/owners`.\n\n## Phase 0 \u2014 Framework, before the controller runs\n\n1. **Security check** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` is on the method, but it is **only enforced when `petclinic.security.enable=true`**. By default the flag is `false`, `DisableSecurityConfig` (`permitAll`) is active, and this check is inert.\n2. **Bean Validation of the request body** (`@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`) \u2014 evaluated before the method body; failures \u2192 `400` via `ExceptionControllerAdvice`. Constraints:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (non-blank), `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)`, `@Email` (nullable)\n   - `address`/`addressLine1`/`addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)` (nullable)\n   - `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{4}$\")` (nullable)\n   - `title` enum coercion; `sharesHousehold` unconstrained\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 `addOwner` idempotency wrapper\n\n3. Read non-blank `Idempotency-Key` header.\n4. If that key was seen before and the prior owner still exists \u2192 **return the original owner with `200 OK`, skipping creation entirely.**\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 `createOwner` \u2192 mapping (`toOwner`)\n\n5. Map DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity (MapStruct); `id` and `pets` ignored.\n6. **Side-effect:** `Owner.setEmail` **lower-cases the email**.\n\n## Phase 3 \u2014 `normalizeAndValidate` (in this exact order; each rejects with `400`)\n\n7. **Normalize address** \u2014 prefers structured `addressLine1`/`addressLine2`, else flat `address`; each field trimmed, whitespace-collapsed, upper-cased, street abbreviations expanded (ST\u2192STREET, etc.); mutates the lines and composed `address`. **Reject 400 if no address at all.**\n8. **Telephone \u2192 E.164** \u2014 assumes `+61` when no `+`, strips non-digits, drops one leading `0`, requires valid length. **Reject 400 if unconvertible;** otherwise **sets** telephone to E.164 form.\n9. **Disposable-email check** \u2014 **reject 400** if the domain is mailinator.com / tempmail.com / guerrillamail.com.\n10. **Postcode validity** \u2014 must be 4 digits within the city's region range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown region accepts any 4 digits; null postcode OK). **Reject 400 if invalid.**\n11. **Future registration date** \u2014 **reject 400** if `registrationDate` is after today.\n12. **Business-day roll** \u2014 default null date to today; roll Saturday/Sunday/public-holidays forward; **set** `registrationDate` to that value.\n\n## Phase 4 \u2014 Rate limit\n\n13. **Daily limit** \u2014 **reject `429`** if \u2265100 active owners already carry that (business-day-adjusted) registration date.\n\n## Phase 5 \u2014 Household assignment & conflict checks\n\n14. Compute `sharesHousehold = Boolean.TRUE.equals(dto.getSharesHousehold())`.\n15. **`assignHousehold`** \u2014 **set** `householdId` = SHA-256(normalizedLastName | postcode)[0:12].\n16. **Household-duplicate check** \u2014 if **not** `sharesHousehold` and an active owner already has the same `householdId` \u2192 **reject `409`**.\n17. **City-capacity check** \u2014 if \u226550 active owners in that city (case-insensitive) \u2192 **reject `409`**. (Not bypassed by `sharesHousehold`.)\n\n## Phase 6 \u2014 `assignDerivedAttributes` (all are field-setting side-effects)\n\n18. **`customerCode`** \u2014 `<REGION>-<HASH8>` from postcode region + SHA-256(telephone + lastName)[0:8], upper-cased, de-duplicated with `-n` suffix against existing active codes.\n19. **`namesakeCount`** \u2014 count of active owners with the same normalized first+last name.\n20. **`bulkSignupWarning`** \u2014 `true` if >80 active owners already on that registration date.\n21. **`householdSize`** \u2014 count of active owners sharing the `householdId`, +1.\n22. **`possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf`** \u2014 if not `sharesHousehold`, find a soft duplicate (same postcode + same normalized lastName but different telephone, lowest id) and flag it.\n\n## Phase 7 \u2014 Persist, audit, respond\n\n23. **`clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`** \u2014 `@Transactional` JPA insert (`ownerRepository.save`). **Entity-level constraints are enforced at flush:** `address` `@NotEmpty`, `city` `@NotEmpty`, `telephone` `@NotEmpty @Pattern(\"^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$\")`, `email` `@Email`, `firstName`/`lastName` `@NotEmpty`, `deleted` non-null. A violation surfaces as `DataIntegrityViolationException` \u2192 **`404`** via the advice.\n24. **Audit log** \u2014 `AUDIT.info(...)` writes the created owner's id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel, membershipNumber.\n25. **`201 Created`** response with a `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header and the `OwnerDto` body.\n26. Back in `addOwner`: if the request carried an `Idempotency-Key` and creation returned `201` with an id, **store `key \u2192 newId`** so a replay returns this owner.\n\n### Notes\n- There are **no** `@PrePersist`/JPA entity listeners, no Spring event publishing, and no email/notification side-effects in the create path. The only non-DB side-effect is the audit log line.\n- The full owner table (`findAllOwners()`) is re-read separately by the daily-limit, customerCode, namesake, bulk-signup, householdSize, city-capacity, household-duplicate and soft-duplicate rules \u2014 i.e. many times per create."
  },
